{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib proof of the main results, Theorems 2.1–2.4, of Erdős, Yau and Yin, \"Rigidity of eigenvalues of generalized Wigner matrices\" (Adv. Math. 229 (2012), arXiv:1007.4652), for real symmetric and complex hermitian generalized Wigner matrices with independent entries, variances summing to one in each row, a spectral gap of the variance matrix and uniform subexponential decay. Theorem 2.1: the strong local semicircle law |m - m_sc| <= (log N)^{4L} / (N eta) down to the optimal scale, its entrywise form, and the bound on the extreme eigenvalues. Theorem 2.2: rigidity of the eigenvalues, |lambda_j - gamma_j| <= (log N)^L min(j, N-j+1)^{-1/3} N^{-2/3} for all j, and the corresponding bound on the counting function, each with probability at least 1 - C exp(-c (log N)^{phi L}). Theorem 2.3: strong local ergodicity of Dyson Brownian motion in the bulk, for times t >= N^{-1+delta+epsilon'}. Theorem 2.4: universality of the largest and of the smallest eigenvalue for two ensembles whose entries have matching first and second moments. No result of another work is assumed; the results the paper cites, in particular the local relaxation flow, are proved in the library from Mathlib.",
